#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/binary.rst:12
#: fe0c163eda174bdaacaf1b0437dbcf7b
msgid ""
"A **binary tree** is a hierarchical data structure where each node has at"
" most two children, referred to as the **left child** and **right "
"child**. A **binary search tree (BST)** is a special type of binary tree "
"that maintains an ordering property: for each node, all values in the "
"left subtree are less than the node's value, and all values in the right "
"subtree are greater."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guide/tree_structures/binary.rst:42
#: 0aa547b43c224f7d8235c299148c9c0a
msgid ""
"Binary trees are fundamental structures used in compilers, expression "
"evaluation, and many search algorithms. BSTs enable efficient searching, "
"insertion, and deletion when properly balanced."
msgstr ""

